---
import { AppDirectoryCard, DocLayout } from '@instancedeck/ui/marketing';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { recipes, lettersFor } from '../../lib/recipes';
import { absoluteUrl } from '../../lib/urls';
import type { Graph } from 'schema-dts';
const schema: Graph = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@graph': [{ '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: absoluteUrl() }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Apps', item: absoluteUrl('apps/') }] }] };
---
<SiteLayout title="App Compatibility Directory – InstanceDeck" description="Inspect InstanceDeck recipes, real launch settings, reported app versions and known limits. Verified, Community and Experimental status stay explicit." schema={schema} ogSlug="apps">
  <DocLayout title="Multi-instance app compatibility" intro="Read the mechanism and the evidence before relying on a profile." breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Apps' }]} linkPrefix="../">
    <p>Verified means the required manual account checks have evidence. Community records reported behavior with provenance. Experimental recipes are incomplete or unverified and are not indexed. No recipe is promoted just because it launches a process.</p>
    <div class="directory">
      {recipes.map((recipe) => <AppDirectoryCard name={recipe.name} letters={lettersFor(recipe.id)} intro={recipe.seo.intro} status={recipe.status} href={`./${recipe.seo.slug}/`} note={recipe.verifiedOn.length ? `Reported ${recipe.verifiedOn.at(-1)!.date} · ${recipe.verifiedOn.at(-1)!.by}` : 'No verified app/Windows version recorded.'} />)}
    </div>
    <h2 id="planned">Configure another app</h2>
    <p>The desktop Custom app editor accepts executable paths, argument templates and non-secret environment variables. Custom isolation starts as Unknown. Built-in generic recipes remain Community while local account smoke testing is deferred.</p>
    <p><a href="../how-it-works/">How isolation works</a> · <a href="../claude-desktop-multiple-accounts/">Claude guide</a> · <a href="../codex-multiple-accounts/">Codex guide</a></p>
  </DocLayout>
</SiteLayout>
<style>.directory { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; margin-top: 48px; } @media (width <= 760px) { .directory { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }</style>
